Extended Error Descriptions:

     Error(211) No directional property data specified for pin
          Indicates that the pin does not have proper INPUT_LOAD, 
          OUTPUT_LOAD, OUTPUT_TYPE, or BIDIRECTIONAL property values to
          specify the pin direction. To fix this error add
          loading values to the chips file for the part.
          This error can be suppressed by adding the
          NO_DIR_CHECK property to the symbol or pin.
          The syntax for the NO_DIR_CHECK property is:
             NO_DIR_CHECK =  TRUE
          You can also suppress this error by turning off the check.
     
     Error(212) Ambiguous directional property data specified on pin
          Indicates that the pin has INPUT_LOAD and OUTPUT load values
          but is not identified as a bidirectional or special pin.
          This error can be fixed by adding the BIDIRECTIONAL or
          OUTPUT_TYPE property to the chips file for the part.
          This error can be suppressed by adding the
          NO_DIR_CHECK property to the symbol or pin.
          The syntax for the NO_DIR_CHECK property is:
             NO_DIR_CHECK =  TRUE
          You can also suppress this error by turning off the check.
     

